

2
00:00:53,494 --> 00:00:57,164
<v CHARLOTTE>Excuse me, Dr Twain. May I speak with you for a minute?

3
00:00:57,164 --> 00:00:59,104
 <v DR TWAIN>Of course, please come in.


4
00:00:59,104 --> 00:01:04,122
<v CHARLOTTE> I’m Charlotte York. I’m considering taking your course in Tourism.

5
00:01:04,122 --> 00:01:08,161
<v DR TWAIN>Right. Well, Charlotte, how can I help you?


6
00:01:17,282 --> 00:01:20,021
<v CHARLOTTE>Would you mind answering some of my questions?


7
00:01:20,021 --> 00:01:22,870
<v DR TWAIN>Absolutely, fire away!

8
00:01:22,870 --> 00:01:32,988
<v CHARLOTTE>Well I have been discussing courses with my parents and they are concerned that I will not be able to get a well-paid job with a degree in Tourism.

9
00:01:32,988 --> 00:01:41,167
<v CHARLOTTE>The reason that I want to study the course is that I have a great interest in the subject and I think I would really enjoy it.

10
00:01:41,167 --> 00:01:47,066
 <v CHARLOTTE>I believe the only way that I will enjoy my life is if I enjoy my career.

11
00:01:47,066 --> 00:01:51,302
<v CHARLOTTE>Happiness is far more important than money, don’t you think?


12
00:01:51,302 --> 00:01:59,544
<v DR TWAIN> Absolutely. I would much rather be happy and poor rather than rich   and miserable. Money cannot buy you happiness.


13
00:01:59,544 --> 00:02:01,300
<v CHARLOTTE>I’m glad you agree.

14
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:04,629
<v DR TWAIN> You needn’t worry about money, Charlotte.

15
00:02:04,629 --> 00:02:14,085
<v DR TWAIN>A large part of the Tourism course is dedicated to teaching students how to manage ﬁnances, a skill that you can apply to your everyday life as well.

16
00:02:14,085 --> 00:02:25,820
<v DR TWAIN>I would also recommend that you take a sideline course in time management, as this can be incredibly useful in efficiently planning your workload. Efficiency is the key to success!


17
00:02:25,820 --> 00:02:27,341
<v CHARLOTTE> I’ll remember that.


18
00:02:27,341 --> 00:02:34,473
<v DR TWAIN> Now I have found that some students have natural talents that really help them to succeed in the course. 

19
00:02:34,473 --> 00:02:40,298
<v DR TWAIN>Communication skills, for example, can be very beneficial. Do you have any strengths?


20
00:02:40,298 --> 00:02:51,007
<v CHARLOTTE> Maths was always my favourite subject at school so I really enjoy solving mathematical problems, however I ﬁnd statistics quite diﬃcult.

21
00:02:51,007 --> 00:02:54,541
<v CHARLOTTE>I have always been very capable and selfsuﬃcient. 

22
00:02:54,541 --> 00:03:03,471
<v CHARLOTTE>I have a lot of conﬁdence in my abilities  and  will  take  the  initiative  in  situations  without  needing  to  depend  on anyone else for their help.


23
00:03:03,471 --> 00:03:10,254
<v DR TWAIN>That’s a really great quality to have and will be particularly useful if  you choose to study Tourism.

24
00:03:10,254 --> 00:03:11,528
<v CHARLOTTE> That’s great.


25
00:03:11,528 --> 00:03:17,200
<v DR TWAIN> I would recommend that you spend some of your time researching the course.

26
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:26,941
<v DR TWAIN>A lot of people who are uneducated on the subject claim that Tourism is a shrinking industry and that it will become irrelevant in the future.

27
00:03:26,941 --> 00:03:33,142
<v DR TWAIN>If you study the published research however, you will see that the truth is quite the opposite.

28
00:03:33,142 --> 00:03:42,865
<v DR TWAIN>The industry has, in fact, grown signiﬁcantly as people have developed an ever-increasing interest in culture and travel. 

29
00:03:42,865 --> 00:03:46,631
<v DR TWAIN>Have you compared the university course with a polytechnic?


30
00:03:46,631 --> 00:03:51,847
<v CHARLOTTE> Yes, I have. I was interested in studying the course in modules. 

31
00:03:51,847 --> 00:03:55,014
<v CHARLOTTE>However, the university doesn’t oﬀer that option.

32
00:03:55,014 --> 00:04:04,425
 <v CHARLOTTE>Don’t have enough funds  to be able to attend an expensive university, so I was relieved to see that the course is quite aﬀordable.

33
00:04:04,425 --> 00:04:16,952
<v CHARLOTTE>I also considered attending a summer school instead of university to save money and so that I could work during the rest of the year, but I really wanted the university experience.

34
00:04:16,952 --> 00:04:20,317
<v DR TWAIN> I think that university would suit you well.

35
00:04:56,759 --> 00:05:02,264
<v DR TWAIN>Now, what about the courses? Are you interested in any of the other subjects on offer?


36
00:05:02,264 --> 00:05:09,361
<v MELANIE>I have looked at a few. I was interested in Travel and Business as it sounds similar to Tourism.

37
00:05:09,361 --> 00:05:17,096
<v DR TWAIN>That is really worth learning, Q26 however, be aware that it is diﬃcult and will demand a lot of your time.

38
00:05:17,096 --> 00:05:19,538
<v MELANIE>OK, that’s good to know.

39
00:05:19,538 --> 00:05:27,318
<v DR TWAIN>You might ﬁnd that an interesting course and it will teach Japanese is you valuable skills in speaking the language.

40
00:05:27,318 --> 00:05:32,744
<v DR TWAIN>Personally, it’s not bad and could be of some help, but not that much.

41
00:05:32,744 --> 00:05:38,205
<v MELANIE>OK, Japanese, got that.. .What about Medical Care?

42
00:05:38,205 --> 00:05:48,788
<v DR TWAIN>Well, if you have time, the course will teach you a lot about curing diseases and illnesses, or dealing with injuries outside, although it’s not essential.

43
00:05:48,788 --> 00:05:51,974
<v CHARLOTTE>So, OK,  if it’s useful, I’ll take it.

44
00:05:51,974 --> 00:06:02,425
<v DR TWAIN>If you enjoy using technology and are worried about fulﬁlling the entry requirements, computing is very relaxed about the skills that applicants must possess.

45
00:06:02,425 --> 00:06:10,342
<v CHARLOTTE>I’m terrible with computers so I’m not sure that I would enjoy that course. How about Public Relations?

46
00:06:10,342 --> 00:06:13,351
<v DR TWAIN>Yes, I would recommend that course.

47
00:06:13,351 --> 00:06:22,430
<v DR TWAIN>It would be related to entering the Tourism industry as it will educate you on how to approach clients and develop associations with them.


48
00:06:22,430 --> 00:06:25,723
<v CHARLOTTE>That’s great! Thank you so much for your help!